#![allow(clippy::excessive_precision)]
//! Golden-parity test for cartalith-engine::generate_terrain -- the tectonic
//! substrate through volcanism/craters/flow(area) segment (reference HTML
//! generate() lines 3339-3369, buildTectonicSubstrate lines 3396-3462),
//! extracted VERBATIM from the reference JS (no deviations needed for this
//! segment -- unlike climate/hydrology, nothing here is deferred/modified).
//!
//! Covers the integration risk this test exists for: does generate_terrain
//! thread each subsystem's output into the next subsystem's input in the
//! same order and shape the JS engine does. Every individual subsystem
//! function this calls already has its own golden test; this one verifies
//! the WIRING between them, which no per-function test can catch.
//!
//! Stops at flow(area) -- climate (temperature/weather/moisture correctors)
//! and river-network topology are each already golden-tested in isolation
//! (cartalith-climate's and cartalith-hydrology's own test suites). Captured
//! by monkey-patching computeFlow to snapshot every field this test checks
//! immediately after its first (area) call, then aborting before climate/
//! carve ever run -- same technique golden_parity_volc_provinces.rs uses,
//! not a hand-stripped re-derivation.
//!
//! **Regenerated 2026-08-15 with `state.volc.provinces = true`**, JS's own
//! real default (WorldParams::defaults now matches it -- see
//! cartalith-native/docs/CHANGELOG.md). The previous version of this fixture
//! deliberately matched this port's then-default (`false`, stampVolcanoesSimple)
//! for a fair same-configuration comparison while the provinces algorithm was
//! still unverified; now that it's golden-tested in its own right
//! (golden_parity_volc_provinces.rs), matching JS's real default here too is
//! the more faithful state to leave this integration test in. plate_id/
//! boundary_mask/stress_field/flexure_field/age_field/heterogeneity_field/
//! resistance_field are computed before volcanism and are bit-identical to
//! the previous fixture, as expected -- only field/volcanic_field/impact_field
//! (volcanism's own writes) and flow_area (reads the post-volcanism field)
//! actually changed.

